# Idle lock and other-device session (do not weaken)

## Inactivity (`InactivityService`)

- Wall-clock time is the source of truth. Last activity and lock deadline are persisted.
- **Never** reset last-activity to “now” on boot, refresh, tab return, or dashboard warmup if a session still exists.
- While the app, web tab, or screen is in the background, the countdown continues. On return: if the lock deadline has passed, **log out immediately** (no new countdown dialog).
- After logout, land on the **enabled** auth screen (password `/login` or fast-login `/fastLogin`), never a blank home.
- The inactivity dialog stays centered (root overlay). Do not let page scroll move it.
- Do not remove, skip, or lengthen these timers in later copies or refactors unless the user explicitly asks.

## Other-device session (`UserSessionCoordinationService`)

- Show «تنبيه جلسة» **only** when the same account signed in from a **different install/device** (web browser profile, phone app, Windows app).
- Same tab refresh, token refresh, and the same install_id must **not** bump-kick or show the dialog.
- The notice must include login type, method, date/time, and location when known.
- «الاستمرار على هذا الجهاز» keeps **this** device; «تسجيل الخروج من هنا» signs out only this device to the correct auth screen.
